Track 2: Canceled Postmark 09-Null
- Story & Context: Within the sorting room of the Lost Mail Bureau, Vesper holds a letter that arrived thirty years late, its ink vibrating as she brushes her thumb over the address written in unfamiliar, angular script. The letter contains a warning about the alignment of the stars, but she realizes the paper is actually a thin sheet of meteorite-infused lead. "Deliver me to the year I never held your hand."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a withered, trembling hand holding a soot-stained envelope, with ancient ink letters beginning to float off the page into the swirling, starlit air.

Track 3: What Does The Mainspring Sing?
- Story & Context: The city elders gather at the crater’s edge to perform the final maintenance ritual, listening to the ground hum in the exact frequency of their own heartbeats. They offer their own mechanical limbs to the earth, transforming the town’s collective consciousness into a singular, eternal machine that will outlast the sky. The soil groaned as the stars turned toward them, acknowledging the debt of the forged iron. "We are the rhythm that refuses to be saved."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A sprawling landscape shot of a town built inside a giant, rusted gear set into the desert floor, with lines of glowing, meteor-infused light spiraling toward a dark, oppressive violet sun.

